# Evidence derived from a class the numeric pin can REVOKE.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is a soundness property, not a shape. `g_boxed_arg`
# is monotone — set once, never cleared — while the pin's demotion is the one
# non-monotone step in the ptype fixpoint. Recording a verdict that depends on a
# pinnable class therefore freezes a fact after its basis has been withdrawn.
#
# Here `f`'s x is gen in round 1 (find_gen_param_use saw `g of x` at a gen
# position, because `takes_dict of y` makes g's parameter gen). arg_class said
# "gen", g#0 was recorded boxed — and the pin then demoted x back to num and
# SPARED y, because y had evidence and x did not. Caller passes a C double,
# callee expects Value*, and emit_args fell through to an env lookup for a name
# that only exists as a C local:
#
#   VM   30 / 6                       rc 0
#   AOT  builds clean, prints 30, then "undefined variable 'x'", rc 1
#
# Worse than t103's failure, which at least refused at build time: this one
# builds, produces correct output, and dies mid-program.
#
# Three consecutive fixes moved WHEN the evidence was recorded — from a separate
# scan, to the widening site, to unconditionally at the widening site — and none
# asked whether the thing recorded was STABLE. arg_gen_grounded is that question:
# literals, void calls and Value*-returning calls cannot be revoked; a local
# cannot (the pin only touches parameters); a parameter can, unless its own class
# is one the pin never demotes or it is itself backed by grounded evidence.

define takes_dict(d) as:
    if d != null:
        print of d.k

define g(y) as:
    if y == null:
        takes_dict of y
        print of "g-null"
    else:
        print of (y * 2)

define f(x) as:
    print of (x * 10)
    g of x

f of 3
